  "notes": "Hi-Tek's bed under a dense delivery, and the word the research uses is chopped rather than looped — so the melody is the busiest on the Rawkus axis (4–8 notes a bar) and its phrase length moves between 2 and 4 bars rather than sitting on one. The documented tempo point is ~98 BPM, which is why `bpm.mode` is 98 and not the middle of the 88–100 band. The other researched parameter is harmonic: i–iv–VII and ii–v–i are real motion, so `extensions` is seventh-led and `harmonicRhythm` favours a chord a bar. The bass \"follows the changes\" rather than the kick, which is `independent_riff` at `followRootsProb` 0.7 — high enough to stay on the roots the chop implies, low enough to move between them. ⚠ `confidence` is medium because the research rates this high-medium: the interview gives gear, method and one tempo, not numbers. ⚠ The INFERRED parameters are the drum densities — `hihat.fillDensity`, `snare.ghost.prob` and the perc lane list. The research says \"layers added over time (shakers, claps) rather than programmed at once\", which is a workflow, not a rate; 0.42 and 0.3 are this axis's middle and should be the first things a listening pass corrects. ⚠ The auto-wah/time-stretch timbre the research names has no vocabulary here; `chopped_vocal` is the nearest existing hint and carries the vowel-like filtered character.",
